1 NAME Stephen /Hopkins/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1581
2 PLAC England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1644
2 PLAC Plymouth
1 NOTE Passenger on the Mayflower, which reached Plymouth in December 1620.
1 NOTE Before Plymouth he sailed for Jamestown in 1609 on the Sea Venture, which wrecked on Bermuda. He was sentenced to death there for mutiny and talked his way into a pardon. The wreck is thought to have inspired Shakespeare's The Tempest.
1 NOTE In Plymouth he served as a go-between with the Wampanoag and died a prosperous shopkeeper in 1644.
1 NOTE Generation 1 of the Mayflower line on Ruby (Brown) White's application.
1 NOTE Source: Mayflower Society application no. 8224 (1985). Years are the standard published dates.
