1 NAME Thomas /Howes/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1601
2 PLAC Norfolk, England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 SEP 1665
2 PLAC Yarmouth
1 NOTE The immigrant. Came from Norfolk with Mary and their sons and was in Salem by about 1637.
1 NOTE A founder of Yarmouth on Cape Cod in 1639, at Nobscussett (now Dennis). Cooper, constable, deputy to the Colony Court and on the Council of War.
1 NOTE His exact parish in Norfolk is unproven; the 1892 Howes genealogy's claim of Morningthorpe has been questioned.
1 NOTE An 1834 monument marks the graves of Thomas and Mary in the Howes Cemetery, Dennis.
1 NOTE Source: The Howes Family in America (J. C. Howes, 1892); his will, Mayflower Descendant vol. 6; minerdescent.com; WikiTree Howes-65.
